 !*********************************************************************
 !
 ! A.KONNOV's detailed reaction mechanism   
 ! 
 ! The choice of the reaction rate constants is given in :  
 !
 ! 01KON/DER1 -
 ! Konnov, A.A., and De Ruyck, J. A Possible New Route for NO Formation  
 ! via N2H3. Combustion Science and Technology.  168: 1-46 (2001). 
 !
 ! 08BAT/KON343 - 
 ! Battin-Leclerc, F., Konnov, A.A., Jaffrezo, J.L., Legrand, M. 
 ! To better understand the formation of short-chain acids in combustion   
 ! systems. Combust. Sci. Technol., 180 (2): 343-370 (2008)
 !
 ! 09KON2093 -
 ! Konnov, A.A. Implementation of the NCN pathway of prompt-NO formation 
 ! in the detailed reaction mechanism.  Combustion and Flame  156: 2093-
 ! 2105 (2009)
 ! 
 ! 10BUR/HAR2864 -
 ! Burluka A.A., Osman H., Harker M., Lawes M., Sheppard C.G.W., Konnov A.A. 
 ! Laminar burning velocities of three C3H6O isomers at atmospheric pressure.  
 ! Fuel, 89: 2864-2872 (2010) 
 !
 ! 12CHA/BRO114 -
 ! Chan, Y.L., Bromly, J.H., Konnov, A.A., Zhang, D.K. 
 ! The Comparative and Combined Effects of Nitric Oxide and Higher Alkanes 
 ! in Sensitising Methane Oxidation .  Combust. Sci. Technol.  184: 114-132
 ! (2012). 
 !
 ! 15ALE/CHR1884 -
 ! Alekseev, V.A., Christensen M., Konnov A.A, The effect of temperature on the 
 ! adiabatic burning velocities of diluted hydrogen flames: a kinetic study using 
 ! an updated mechanism. Combust. Flame,  162: 1884-1898 (2015).
 !
 ! 15KON3753 - 
 ! Konnov, A.A. On the role of excited species in hydrogen combustion.  
 ! Combust. Flame,  162: 3753-3770 (2015). 
 !
 ! 16NIL/KON2443 -
 ! Nilsson E.J.K., Konnov A.A., Role of HOCO chemistry in syngas combustion.  
 ! Energy and Fuels,  30: 2443-2457 (2016) 
 !
 ! 16CHR/KON12 -
 ! Christensen M., Konnov A.A., Laminar burning velocity of acetic acid + air  
 ! flames. Combust. Flame,  170: 12-29 (2016)
 ! 
 ! 16FOM/ZAV198 - 
 ! Fomin A., Zavlev T., Alekseev V.A., Rahinov I., Cheskis S., Konnov A.A. 
 ! Experimental and modelling study of 1CH2 in premixed very rich methane  
 ! flames. Combust. Flame,  171: 198-210 (2016) 
 !
 ! 16CHR/NIL6709 -
 ! Christensen M., Nilsson E.J.K., Konnov A.A., A systematically updated 
 ! detailed kinetic model for CH2O and CH3OH combustion. Energy and Fuels 
 ! 30: 6709-6726 (2016) 
 !
 ! 17CHR/KON97 -
 ! Christensen M., Konnov A.A., Laminar burning velocity of diacetyl + air 
 ! flames. Further assessment of combustion chemistry of ketene. Combust. 
 ! Flame, 178: 97-110 (2017)
 !
 ! 18SEM/SHU273 -
 ! Semenikhin A. S., Shubina E. G., Savchenkova A. S., Chechet I. V., 
 ! Matveev S. G., Konnov, A.A., Mebel A. M. Mechanism and rate constants of  
 ! the CH3 + CH2CO reaction:A theoretical study. Int.J.Chem.Kinet., 50:
 ! 273-284 (2018).
 ! 
 ! 18CAP/ALE11 -
 ! Capriolo G., Alekseev V.A., Konnov A.A., An experimental and kinetic study of 
 ! propanal oxidation. Combust. Flame, 197: 11-21 (2018). 
 !
 ! 19SAV/SEM387 -
 ! Savchenkova A.S., Semenikhin A.S., Chechet I.V., Matveev S.G., Konnov, A.A., 
 ! Mebel A.M. Mechanism and rate constants of the CH2 + CH2CO reactions in triplet
 ! and singlet states: A theoretical study. J. Comput. Chem., 40: 387-399 (2019). 
 !
 ! 19KON14 -
 ! Konnov A.A., Yet another kinetic mechanism for hydrogen combustion. Combust.Flame 203:
 ! 14-22 (2019). 
 !
 ! 19NIL/van904 -
 ! Nilsson E.J.K., van Sprang A., Larfeldt J., Konnov A.A., Effect of natural 
 ! gas composition on the laminar burning velocities at elevated temperatures. 
 ! Fuel,  253: 904-909 (2019). 
 !
 ! 20SAV/SEM28 -
 ! A. S. Savchenkova, A. S. Semenikhin, I. V. Chechet, S. G. Matveev, A. M. Mebel,
 ! Konnov, A.A., Revisiting diacetyl and acetic acid flames: the role of the ketene + OH 
 ! reaction. Combust. Flame, 218: 28-41 (2020). 
 !
 ! 20CAP/KON189 -
 ! Capriolo, G., Konnov A.A., Combustion of propanol isomers: experimental and 
 ! kinetic modelling study. Combust. Flame, 218: 189-204 (2020). 
 !
 ! Other SQUIB or comments or absence of it means Work-in-progress.
 !
 !*********************************************************************
